sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SC as Scheduler
    participant RC as Reconciliation Service
    participant SP as Shopify
    participant PM as Paymob
    participant BO as Bosta (COD)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    actor FIN as Finance

    Note over SC,FIN: Requirement 4.1, 12.3 - three sources of payment truth must agree.<br/>90% of orders are Cash on Delivery, so Bosta - not the PSP - holds most of the money.

    SC->>RC: nightly reconciliation run

    par pull each source
        RC->>SP: orders + financial status
        SP-->>RC: order totals, payment method, gift cards
    and
        RC->>PM: settled transactions for the period
        PM-->>RC: transaction id, amount, status, fees
    and
        RC->>BO: COD collection report
        BO-->>RC: collected amounts, remittance batches
    end

    RC->>RC: match on order reference + amount

    Note right of RC: Payment Method in the sheet has 13<br/>distinct spellings including<br/>"cash on Delivery (COD)" and<br/>"CAsh on Delivery (COD)".<br/>Normalisation happens here, once.

    alt fully matched
        RC->>DB: mark payment reconciled
    else amount mismatch
        RC->>DB: flag EXCEPTION (short / over collection)
        RC->>FIN: exception queue
        Note right of FIN: Partial COD collection is common.<br/>The exception queue is the control -<br/>not a spreadsheet comparison.
    else COD collected but order not Delivered
        RC->>DB: flag status conflict
        Note right of DB: Usually a late Bosta webhook.<br/>Auto-resolves on next run,<br/>escalates if it persists 48h.
    else Delivered but no collection after SLA
        RC->>FIN: chase 3PL remittance
    end

    opt combined payment methods
        RC->>RC: split across tenders<br/>(Paymob + COD, Gift Card + COD, Store Credit + COD)
        Note right of RC: 45 Gift Card + COD and 25 Paymob + COD<br/>rows exist. Item-level margin needs the<br/>split, not just the order total.
    end

    RC->>RC: allocate collected amount to ORDER_ITEMS<br/>pro-rata by item value
    RC->>DB: update item-level payment tracking (Req 2.1)

    RC->>FIN: publish reconciliation report<br/>(matched / exceptions / ageing)
    FIN->>DB: resolve exceptions with audit trail
